## 2. Phase 1: Security & Identity Remediation (P0)
**Objective:** Eliminate critical security vulnerabilities and hardcoded bypasses to establish a robust, production-grade architecture (immediate deployment is not the priority, but creating a secure foundational baseline is).

| Task ID | Component | Remediation Action | Est. | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **1.1** | **Secrets Management** | Remove all live credentials from **both** `.env` AND `supabase/docker/.env`. Add both to `.gitignore`. Create `.env.example` with placeholder values. Rotate all exposed keys. | 2h | Todo |
| **1.2** | **Mock OTP Gating** | Wrap the `0000` OTP bypass in `IntakeForm.tsx` (Line 62) inside a `process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development'` guard. | 1h | Todo |
| **1.3** | **SSO Hardcoding Fix** | Replace hardcoded `providerId` and `redirectTo` auth URLs with environment variables. | 30m | Todo |
| **1.4** | **Session Governance** | Update `src/middleware.ts`, `auth/callback/route.ts`, and `actions/complaints.ts` to use `getUser()` instead of `getSession()`.<br><br>**Elaboration (`getSession` vs `getUser`):**<br>`getSession()` only looks at the session cookie locally in the Next.js server. It does not verify with the database if the user was deleted or disabled. Basically, it's fast but insecure.<br>`getUser()` physically makes an API request to the Supabase Auth server (GoTrue) on every page load to guarantee the user's token is still valid. It is secure, but it is heavily dependent on network connectivity. | 2.5h | Todo |

> [!WARNING]
> **Task 1.4 — Risk Note (Elaborated):**
> The local Supabase GoTrue Auth service has a known bug or resource constraint in this project where it frequently returns `504 Gateway Timeout` errors when Next.js tries to talk to it via the `@supabase/ssr` library.
> Because of these timeouts, a previous developer bypassed `@supabase/ssr` in `login/page.tsx`, directly manipulating `document.cookie` via JavaScript on the client side to forcefully log the user in without timing out.
> If we blindly switch the entire app's middleware to use `getUser()` (which makes heavy API calls to that same GoTrue service), the whole application might crash with 504 timeouts. Therefore, before we finalize this change, we MUST test if `getUser()` can run against the local Docker Supabase without timing out.

